    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <actual value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3 Fisherfolk Ambassadors: 2 males and 1 female (rightsholder representatives) wrote advocacy letters to the district and Kammengo sub-county to influence social service delivery. This was achieved through consensual alliances that the Fisherfolk Ambassadors formed with local leaders like the LCs, Area Counselors who supportively endorsed on the letter to be able to reach the duty bearers.
Letter 1 was addressed to the DHO, sharing evidence about a lack of psychiatric drugs and condoms at Butoolo HCIII and prompting for district action to restock the facility with those services.
Letter 2 was addressed to the DEO sharing absence of accountability by the Headteacher in running St Martin Buyiga Primary School, and requesting for a change of the Head Teacher.
Letter 3 was addressed to Senior Administrative Secretary (SAS) at Kammengo Sub-county, sharing the need to revamp the community borehole in Mukajja Village</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
