     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
     <actual value="3">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A youth focal health worker was designated to attend to the needs of youth rightsholders who accessed ART services at Buyiga HCIII.

Youth rightsholders who access ART services at the Buyiga HCIII, have identified their peers, who, due to stigma, do not access ART services. These youth have reached out to others through peer to peer home visits.
Rightsholders living with mental disability and epilepsy have identified their peers and raised awareness about the regular psychiatric clinic at Butoolo HCIII. This has  upscaled demand and access to psychiatric services. The regular psychiatric clinic which started off with 9 rightsholders, now registers on average, 15 to 20 rightsholders

These were achieved by the the presence of a peer support network by the Fisherfolk Ambassadors who encouraged peers to connect, share experiences, and identify others in similar situations, fostering a sense of community.
All rightsholders living with disabilities now capture their details in the facility register at Butoolo HCIII when they visit the health facility; which has continuously supported the Facility In-Charge to request for drugs,  services or lobby for support as informed by rightsholder data in the facility register. This was achieved by the appreciationof the use of data in advocacy by both rightsholders and social actors.</narrative>
      </comment>
